            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="NAP03" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Lady</roleName>
                        <forename>Sarah</forename>
                        <surname>Napier</surname>
                        <addName>née Lennox</addName>
                        <addName>Bunbury</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1745-02-14">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1826-08-26"/>
                    <occupation>noblewoman</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin records her death - although he enters it on
    the 20th. There are other refs to a 'S Napier' , although fewer than the many to Mrs Napier, and there are a range of other initials associated with Napier. We assume these refer to others: 
    Lady Sarah Napier was extremely aristocratic (she was <persName key="FOX01">Charles James Fox's</persName> aunt), did not move in Godwin's circles and was in poor health by the 1810s,
  when the references appear. Only her death has been coded.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
